This stage implements a source-assisted compatibility contract for three VS Code API value classes. The candidate module is newly written and imports no Microsoft runtime.

The retained authoritative source snapshots are copyright Microsoft Corporation and licensed under the MIT License. Exact copyright headers remain in every source file, and the full license is preserved in `source/LICENSE.txt.snapshot` (SHA-256 `9480271317925265e806a9a196aaa33410a962fa9d4d1e248a4a5187bc8c9df9`). Preserve those notices and the license with redistributed source snapshots or derivative compatibility material.

The source-only verification oracle evaluates exact selected Microsoft source bodies after the disclosed TypeScript/module composition steps. This verification tooling is separate from the new runtime module. The original VS Code native executable, workbench and extension host are not redistributed or evaluated here.
